  "answer": "The Enterprise onboarding range in the playbook is **8–10 weeks** [NL-005-S02][NL-031-S02]. The observed Enterprise average/median duration is **8.7 weeks**, calculated from the sample customers (8.2 + 8.4 + 9.5 ÷ 3) and consistent with the Q2 Business Metrics Report [NL-031-S03][NL-012-S06]. This observed duration sits within the playbook range.\n\nBy comparison, simpler plans are much faster: Starter/SMB averages **3.5 weeks**, and Growth/Mid-Market averages **5.2 weeks** [NL-012-S06][NL-031-S02][NL-031-S03].\n\nThe Enterprise duration is longer because Enterprise onboarding involves security reviews, custom data-processing agreements, SSO/SAML/OIDC setup, custom data-retention configurations, strict permission mapping to replicate internal folder hierarchies, and OCR processing of scanned legacy PDFs [NL-005-S02][NL-031-S02][NL-005-S09]. The main delay drivers overall are permission mapping (45% of delays), source ingestion cleanup (30%), and OCR processing (25%) [NL-012-S06]. Simpler Starter and Growth plans do not require complex RBAC, deep directory integration, or extensive security/compliance work, so they go live more quickly [NL-012-S06][NL-031-S02].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer  \nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
